Commit:     Viche Recovery Steward <recovery-steward@viche.local>
CommitDate: Sat Nov 7 17:40:33 2026 +0000

    Fail closed on unverifiable case closure provenance
    
    Every office runs as one Unix identity and the whole state root is writable
    by it, so a JSON artifact naming "clerk" or "judiciary" asserts provenance
    rather than proving it. Act 23 §5.1/§5.2 therefore cannot be satisfied by the
    current artifact scheme, and the previous code closed cases on exactly that
    self-assertion.
    
    Keep all content validation (case identity, accepted office, ordering against
    the observed failure, in-root regular-file evidence with matching sha256), but
    classify any resulting artifact as closure_eligible=false and preserve it as
    unverified_verification_claim for audit. Cases stay open and visible until a
    verifier identity anchored outside the writable root exists.
    
    Tests now assert both directions: a well-formed self-authored artifact is
    retained for audit but cannot close a case, and continuity receipts alone
    likewise cannot close one.

